# docs/ is deliberately PARTIALLY tracked. The rule:
#   engine design docs are tracked; reference material and agent tooling are not.
# Tracked (do not add ignores that would catch these):
#   docs/RetroFE/Layout-Hot-Reload-Blueprint.md
#   docs/RetroFE/RetroFE Modernization and Performance.md
# Ignored below: upstream manuals, wiki mirrors and the binaries that come with
# them. This repo is already ~1.2 GB of git objects, so reference material that
# can be re-downloaded stays out of history.
docs/RetroFE_Wiki/
docs/RetroFE/retrofe_clean_manual.md
docs/RetroFE/retrofe_knowledge_base.md
docs/RetroFE/*.pdf

# Rust build artifacts (RustCore/target reaches 2+ GB with bundled DuckDB)
RetroFE/Source/RustCore/target/

# Shell-redirect debris, e.g. unquoted `pip install requests>=2.31.0`
=*

